---
description: Keep Filament filter labels consistent, especially date ranges
globs: app/Filament/**/*.php
alwaysApply: false
---

# Filter labels

Date range filters always use **Start Date** and **End Date**. Never From, To, Until, or mixed casing.

```php
// BAD
DatePicker::make('from')->label('From'),
DatePicker::make('until')->label('Until'),

// GOOD
DatePicker::make('start_date')->label('Start Date'),
DatePicker::make('end_date')->label('End Date'),
```

If the same form has more than one date range, prefix with the data it filters:

```php
DatePicker::make('imported_from')->label('Import Start Date'),
DatePicker::make('imported_to')->label('Import End Date'),
DatePicker::make('created_from')->label('Create Start Date'),
DatePicker::make('created_to')->label('Create End Date'),
```

Reuse existing labels for the same concept (`Calling list`, `Lead type`, `Health`, `Last Disp`). Do not invent a second name for a filter that already exists on another page.
